**Default value:** `sortObjects` defaults to `true`. It is declared in the base `Renderer` class at `renderers/common/Renderer.js:213` (`this.sortObjects = true;`), with the JSDoc `@default true` at line 211. The WebGPU renderer inherits this via `WebGPURenderer extends Renderer` (`renderers/webgpu/WebGPURenderer.js:28`) and does not override the property.

**What changes when it is true:** In the shared render loop, after the render list is populated and finalized (`renderList.begin()` / `finish()` at `renderers/common/Renderer.js:1885–1889`), the code branches on the flag at `renderers/common/Renderer.js:1891–1895`:

```js
if ( this.sortObjects === true ) {
    renderList.sort( this._opaqueSort, this._transparentSort );
}
```

When `sortObjects` is `true`, the renderer sorts the opaque and transparent render lists before drawing — ordering objects so transparency is rendered back-to-front. When it is `false`, the render list is drawn in the order the scene was traversed, with no sorting pass.

The sort functions `_opaqueSort` / `_transparentSort` default to `null` (`renderers/common/Renderer.js:446, 455`) and are configurable via `setOpaqueSort` / `setTransparentSort` (lines 2284–2299); `null` means the renderer's default sort is used.

**Rebuild detection in `ClippingContext`** (`renderers/common/ClippingContext.js`) relies on two version counters:

1. **`this.version`** (line 41) — the context's own version counter, initialized to `0`. It is incremented at line 234 inside `update()`, but only when new clipping planes are actually added to the local plane arrays (i.e., when `dstClippingPlanes.length !== offset + l`, line 216). On increment, `cacheKey` is also regenerated at line 235: `` `${this.id}:${this.intersectionPlanes.length}:${this.unionPlanes.length}` ``.

2. **`this.parentVersion`** (line 107) — stores the last-observed version of the parent context, initialized to `null`. It is updated at line 178 inside `update()` when the parent's version differs from the stored value.

**Parent-change detection** is purely version-counter comparison, not a callback or reference check. In `ClippingContext.update()` (lines 170–239), the check at line 174 is:

```js
if ( parentContext.version !== this.parentVersion ) {
    this.intersectionPlanes = Array.from( parentContext.intersectionPlanes );
    this.unionPlanes = Array.from( parentContext.unionPlanes );
    this.parentVersion = parentContext.version;
}
```

So when the parent's `version` counter changes, the child copies the parent's `intersectionPlanes` and `unionPlanes` arrays and records the new `parentVersion`. Combined with the local version increment on plane changes, these counters let the context know when its cached clip data is stale and must be rebuilt.
